      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-224058",
      ":question/problem": "Consider three random samples from three populations having the same variance. The following table gives the sample sizes $n$ and the sample variances $s^{2}$ for each sample. Rounded to two decimal places, what is the pooled estimate of the variance?\n\n|  | Sample 1 | Sample 2 | Sample 3 |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $n$ | $14$ | $16$ | $25$ |\n| $s^{2}$ | $1.3$ | $1.1$ | $1.0$ |\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
