      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-224416",
      ":question/problem": "Consider four random samples from four populations having the same variance. The following table gives the sample sizes $n$ and the sample variances $s^{2}$ for each sample. Rounded to two decimal places, what is the pooled estimate of the variance?\n\n|  | Sample 1 | Sample 2 | Sample 3 | Sample 4 |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $n$ | $12$ | $14$ | $15$ | $16$ |\n| $s^{2}$ | $4.2$ | $5.3$ | $4.7$ | $5.1$ |\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
